course: dictionary
lesson: 5749
title: Many meanings of lovely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Lovely» is a word people use every day. Its main meaning is very nice, pleasant or beautiful. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «A small, lovely sign of respect» means a small, nice sign, something pleasant to see.
explain: «Lovely» can also mean kind and friendly. Think about what it describes. In «she's a lovely person», lovely is about how someone behaves, not how something looks.
explain: In some places, people say «Lovely, thanks!» to mean great, or to say thank you. Check by swapping in another word: «Great, thanks!» still makes sense, so that is the meaning here.
fact: «Lovely» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «a lovely day» or «a lovely person».
fact: The comparative forms are lovelier and loveliest.
fact: «Lovely» means very nice, pleasant or beautiful, and it can also mean kind and friendly.
fact: «Lovely, thanks!» is a common, polite reply in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, and it means great.
fact: Slang: «lush» (Wales) also means lovely.
exercise: «At festive dinners even kids raise their juice and shout gānbēi! (cheers!), a small, lovely sign of respect.» What does lovely mean here? | Very sad | Very loud | *Very nice and pleasant | Very expensive
exercise: Someone passes you the salt and says, «Lovely, thanks!» What does lovely mean? | Very heavy | Please go away | Be quiet | *Great, thank you
exercise: «Animation is a lovely trick on your brain.» Which word could replace lovely with the same meaning? | Heavy | *Wonderful | Painful | Boring
test: «She's a lovely person.» What does lovely mean here? | Very cold | *Kind and friendly | Very lost | Very loud
test: Which is the correct comparative form of lovely? | lovelest | lovliest | *lovelier | lovelyer
exam: Which meaning of lovely fits «It was lovely to see you again»? | Very heavy | Very old | Very dark | *Very nice and pleasant
